\begin_layout Standard
You should indicate the path to the database as the first argument.
 Providing the optional argument, verbose, causes the read function to summarize
 the tables created, their fields and their sizes.
 Finally, a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

R environment
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 that contains the database tables is returned.
 (If you are unfamiliar with environments, you can think of it as data frame.
 If fact, 
\emph on
ENV$locus_table
\emph default
 will access the 
\emph on
locus_table
\emph default
 variable from ENV as though fetching an 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

observation
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 from a data frame.
 The difference is when you change a data frame passed to a function, the
 change does not affect the original data frame.
 Only the local function value is changed; the change is forgotten when
 the function exits.
 If you change the data in an environment passed to a function, the change
 is permanent.) 
\end_layout

